      <span class="eyebrow">About Moringa Powder</span>
      <h2 class="h-sec">What is Moringa <span class="it" style="color:var(--c)">powder?</span></h2>
      <p>Moringa powder is made by gently drying and milling the leaves of <i>Moringa oleifera</i>, a fast-growing tree native to the foothills of the Himalayas in northern India. In Indian kitchens the leaves, often called drumstick leaves, are cooked as a vegetable; milling them into a fine powder makes them easy to use every day.</p><p>Veda Apothecary Moringa Powder has exactly one ingredient — Moringa leaf — with no additives, fillers or preservatives. It is milled in small batches to protect its vivid green color and fresh, grassy aroma. A 6 g serving provides 120 mg of calcium (9% DV) and 1.7 mg of iron (9% DV), alongside 1 g of dietary fiber, as listed on the Supplement Facts panel.</p>
      <table class="facts"><caption class="sr-only">Moringa Powder key facts</caption><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Botanical name</th><td><i>Moringa oleifera</i></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Plant part</th><td>Leaf</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Net weight</th><td>8 oz (227 g)</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Servings per container</th><td>about 38</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Ingredients</th><td>One — leaf powder only</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Origin</th><td>Product of India</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Distributed by</th><td>Old Soul Goods Inc.</td></tr></tbody></table>
    </div>
  </section>

